# WIP preservation (always-on)

**Non-negotiable:** uncommitted work must never be destroyed. A branch or worktree may be
closed only when its tree is clean, or when the changes are preserved on a named WIP branch.

## Why this rule exists

On 2026-11-21 the auth brand-bar alignment and the dashboard Profile modal "On this device"
card were found missing from production. Both had been written in the 2026-11-16 batch, but
only existed in `stash@{1}` (WIP on `perf/fix-boot-counting`) and an unmerged feature branch.
An unrelated release shipped without them. This rule prevents a repeat.

## Hard rules

1. Never run `git stash`, `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd`, `git branch -D`,
   `git branch --delete --force`, or `git worktree remove --force` while any worktree is dirty.
2. Preserve first: `bun run wip:save <short-name>`. It commits the changes to
   `wip/<date>-<short-name>` and returns to the original branch.
3. A stash is not storage. If a stash is unavoidable, label it
   (`git stash push -m "<owner> <date> <why>"`) and move it to a branch in the same session:
   `git stash branch wip/<date>-<name> 'stash@{0}'`.
4. Before closing a session, or cleaning branches/worktrees, run `bun run wip:audit`.
5. Never remove a worktree that has `git status --porcelain` output. Preserve, then remove.
6. A branch merged into `develop` can still carry unique commits. Check with
   `bun run branch:audit`; the `branch-lifecycle` rule still applies.

## Scope

Every agent (Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode) and every human working in this repo.

## Hooks and tools

| Tool                                  | What it does                                                              |
| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `scripts/dev/wip-guard-lib.sh`        | Shared shell guard: detects dirty trees and blocks destructive commands   |
| `.cursor/hooks/guard-shell.sh`        | Cursor `beforeShellExecution` deny                                        |
| `.claude/hooks/guard-shell.sh`        | Claude Code `PreToolUse` deny                                             |
| `.opencode/plugins/gfm-ai-tooling.ts` | Routes OpenCode bash through the same Claude hook                         |
| `bun run wip:save <name>`             | Commits dirty work to `wip/<date>-<name>`, returns to the original branch |
| `bun run wip:audit`                   | Lists stashes and dirty worktrees; `--strict` exits 1 when found          |

Owner override for one command only: include `wipsafe` (or `WIP_PRESERVED=1`) after the user
explicitly says the work is disposable. Never override on your own initiative.

## Recovery

- `bun run wip:audit` to find the work.
- `git stash list` and `git stash show -p 'stash@{n}'` to inspect a stash.
- `git stash branch wip/recover 'stash@{n}'` to turn a stash into a branch.
- `git reflog` for a lost commit; `git branch <name> <sha>` to restore it.
- Deleted branches: tip SHAs are recorded in
  `docs/archive/operations/branch-cleanup-audit.md`.

